  "notes": [
    "Routing and account numbers are source numeric-only strings, preserving leading zeros. Tax identifiers retain the original9–30-character source string including the foreign-organization example; no stricter EIN/SSN policy is invented.",
    "Agency, payee, financial institution and authorized official remain distinct roles/entities. Agency fields are supplied context, not applicant-entered answers.",
    "All three addresses reuse the existing GlobalLibrary address question and its country activity/requiredness. Optional agency address/name groups are absent until supplied; partial objects must satisfy their source required members.",
    "The authorized-official title permits60characters; the45-character person/title bank question is an explicit nonfit. Financial institution name is55characters and is not organization/name60.",
    "Despite its Signature and Title heading, the original XSD group contains only name, title and phone. No signature value, consent or bank authorization service is invented.",
    "Original source privacy text is retained. Examples are synthetic; source instructions calling for a bank/agency to complete fields remain separate from authentic service integration."
  ],
  "risks": [
    "Country changes retain inactive values under the existing shared address behavior. Any eventual XML projection must respect the original State/Province choice and active-country rules; this definition does not introduce a serializer.",
    "Agency-provided fields require authentic agency context in production; the preview cannot produce or verify it."
  ],
